From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:04:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Use USB security keys for WebAuthn through
 libfido2

WebAuthn ceremonies can now use security keys on USB, on macOS. Yubico's
libfido2 speaks CTAP2 and CTAP1/U2F to them over HID, with both PIN
protocols, and is already in vcpkg's baseline under the BSD-2-Clause
license, with libcbor and the OpenSSL and zlib we already have.

While a ceremony waits, discovery polls for FIDO HID devices on a thread
of its own and asks each new one what it supports. libfido2 blocks while
a key waits for a touch, so each operation runs on its own thread, which
opens the key, makes its request, and closes the key again, and the UI
process cancels it with CTAPHID_CANCEL. Waiting for the user to touch a
key, to choose it before entering its PIN, uses CTAP 2.1's
authenticatorSelection, which libfido2 imitates on older keys.

Linux would work the same way, but libfido2's port needs libudev's
headers there, which the CI image doesn't have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
